00:46:25,263 --> 00:46:31,263
Son of Dracula is a 1974 British musical film directed by Freddie
Francis and starring Harry Nilsson and Ringo Starr.

10
00:51:34,736 --> 00:51:40,736
It was produced by Starr and released in 1974 by Apple Films.

11
00:56:44,210 --> 00:56:50,210
It is also the title of a soundtrack released in conjunction with the film.

12
01:01:53,684 --> 01:01:59,684
Keith Moon of The Who and John Bonham of Led Zeppelin both appear in the
film, alternating as the drummer in Count Downe's band.

13
01:07:03,157 --> 01:07:09,157
Other band members include Klaus Voormann (another old friend of Starr), Peter Frampton, an uncredited
Leon Russell, and the regular Rolling Stones horn section of Bobby Keys and Jim Price.

14
01:12:12,631 --> 01:12:18,631
In the film, Count Dracula is assassinated, and his son Count Downe is
supposed to inherit his control over the Netherworld.

15
01:17:22,105 --> 01:17:28,105
Instead, the son wishes to become mortal and asks Dr.

16
01:22:31,578 --> 01:22:37,578
Abraham Van Helsing to help him transform into an ordinary human.

17
01:27:41,052 --> 01:27:47,052
The film explores themes of based on novel or book,
vampire, reincarnation, romance, gothic horror.

18
01:32:50,526 --> 01:32:56,526
The tone is dark and emotional.
